 ## 1. Domain
 
 | Entity | What it is (one line) | Owns these facts | Identity | Traces to (screen, flow, rule) |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| watchlist_items | one ticker one user follows | which tickers a user follows, when added | bigint identity | spec AC1-AC4 |
 
 **Relationships:**
 | Child | Parent | Cardinality | ON DELETE | Why |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| watchlist_items | auth.users | many to one | CASCADE | a deleted account leaves no orphan rows |
 
 ## 2. Invariants in the database
 
 | Table | Invariant | Mechanism (NOT NULL / CHECK / FK / UNIQUE / trigger) | What breaks without it |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| watchlist_items | a ticker is 1-5 capital letters | CHECK `ticker ~ '^[A-Z]{1,5}$'` | junk tickers reach the provider calls |
+| watchlist_items | a user follows a ticker once | UNIQUE (user_id, ticker) | duplicate rows; the route maps 23505 to 409 |
+| watchlist_items | every row has an owner | NOT NULL + FK to auth.users | rows no policy can ever show |
 
 ## 3. Access model (RLS)
 
 | Table | Role | Operation | Policy (USING / WITH CHECK) | Allow check | Deny check |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| watchlist_items | authenticated | SELECT | USING `(select auth.uid()) = user_id` | owner sees own row | other user sees 0 of owner's rows |
+| watchlist_items | authenticated | INSERT | WITH CHECK `(select auth.uid()) = user_id` | owner adds own row | insert for another user refused 42501, no row added |
+| watchlist_items | authenticated | DELETE | USING `(select auth.uid()) = user_id` | owner removes own row | other user's delete removes 0 rows, row still there |
+| watchlist_items | authenticated | UPDATE | none (an item is added or removed, never edited) | n/a | owner's update changes nothing |
+| watchlist_items | anon | all | none (secure defaults revoke table access) | n/a | anon select refused 42501 |
 
